# Prettier owns the stylesheets only: this is what keeps app.css from being
# checked in minified again. JS/JSX formatting is left to ESLint and review so
# that behaviour changes stay readable in diffs.
*
# `*` also matches the directories on the way down, and a file inside an
# ignored directory cannot be re-included: each directory needs its own line.
# Until 2026-10-13 `src/` had none, so every sheet read `ignored: true` and
# `format:check` passed without opening one.
!src/
!src/styles/
!src/styles/**/
!src/styles/**/*.css

# Minified output of `npm run build:critical`, sliced verbatim out of the built
# stylesheet. Reformatting it would break the staleness guard in vite.config.js,
# which proves each inlined rule still appears in the sheet byte for byte.
src/styles/critical.generated.css
